{%- comment -%}
  Related products — the cross-sell that closes the product page. Extracted
  from sections/main-product.liquid, where it rendered inline after the tabs
  (the block that was main-product.liquid:71-88).

  WHY IT IS ITS OWN SECTION. The customer voices wall now sits on the product
  page, and it has to sit between the purchase decision and the cross-sell: fit
  evidence reaches the buyer before four more pairs of trousers do. While this
  block lived inside `main` no section order could put anything between the tabs
  and this grid — the order ["main","voices","related"] can. Nothing else about
  the block changed in the move; the section id is `related`.

  IT HIDES ITSELF RATHER THAN DRAWING PLACEHOLDERS, and that is the behaviour it
  had inline, kept deliberately. `related.products.size > 1` means the catalogue
  holds something other than the piece being viewed. With an empty store there
  is no cross-sell to make, and a row of placeholder cards under "You may also
  like" would claim there is one — so this is not the grid-is-the-point case
  that new arrivals and the catalogue are, where the placeholder cards exist to
  make the columns, gaps and card proportions reviewable before import. Here an
  absent recommendation is the honest state.

  DEVIATION FROM THE BLOCK IT REPLACES — two-up on the phone. The grid was
  `sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4`, so it stacked one card to a row below `sm`
  while the catalogue and new arrivals ran two: the same card rendered at three
  different sizes on three routes. The gap set is now byte-identical to
  new-arrivals.liquid:48 and main-collection.liquid:48. The `sizes` hint follows
  the grid — two-up means each card is roughly 45vw on a phone, not 90vw, which
  is what stops image_tag picking a candidate twice the size needed.

  The heading is an h2 under the h1 that `main` puts on the product title, and
  the cards keep product-card's default h3, so the document outline is the one
  the block had inline. It is a section setting so the client can retitle it,
  falling back to the interface string in locales/en.default.json — which is
  what it rendered before there was a setting at all.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign related = collections[section.settings.related_collection] | default: collections.all
  assign limit = section.settings.count
  assign default_heading = 'product.related_heading' | t
  assign heading = section.settings.heading | default: default_heading
  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 1024px) 23vw, 45vw'
-%}

{%- if related.products.size > 1 -%}
  <section
    aria-labelledby="related-heading"
    class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-content flex-col gap-8 px-gutter pb-section pt-block-lg"
  >
    <div data-reveal>
      <h2 id="related-heading" class="font-body text-h2 leading-h2">{{ heading }}</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-4 gap-y-8 sm:gap-x-7 sm:gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
      {%- for entry in related.products -%}
        {%- if entry.handle != product.handle and shown < limit -%}
          <div data-reveal>{% render 'product-card', product: entry, sizes: card_sizes %}</div>
          {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Related products",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Hides itself when the catalogue holds nothing but the piece being viewed — there is no recommendation to make, so none is drawn." },
    { "type": "collection", "id": "related_collection", "label": "Related from", "info": "Leave empty to draw from every product." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's own wording." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "count", "label": "Products shown", "min": 2, "max": 8, "step": 1, "default": 4 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Related products" }]
}
{% endschema %}
